  "issue_number": 3383,
  "issue_title": "Add a block-time / chain-activity sparkline strip to the home page",
  "issue_body": "## Context\n\n`HeroKpis` in `apps/ui/src/routes/index.tsx` (lines 322-414) renders the homepage's \"Registry pulse\" card with a `SubnetPulseGrid`, a \"Healthy now\" stat (no series \u2014 `/api/v1/health` exposes no per-hour history), and a \"Freshness\" stat with a real sparkline built from `/api/v1/freshness` per-source ages. There is no block-time / chain-activity series anywhere in `index.tsx` \u2014 confirmed by grep, zero references to `chainActivityQuery`, `ChainActivity`, `block_count`, or `extrinsic_count` in that file. `chainActivityQuery(window)` (`apps/ui/src/lib/metagraphed/queries.ts:2297`) already fetches `/api/v1/chain/activity` and is consumed today on `apps/ui/src/routes/explorer.tsx` (`ExplorerDashboard`, lines 225-354) via `MiniSeries` cells for extrinsics/blocks/events/success-rate/unique-signers. The home page has no chain-direct signal at all \u2014 only registry/freshness/health metadata.\n\n## Requirement\n\nAdd a small chain-activity sparkline strip to the home page hero, driven by the already-wired `chainActivityQuery`, so a visitor sees real block/extrinsic activity (not just registry metadata) without leaving Home.\n\n## Deliverable\n\n- File to change: `apps/ui/src/routes/index.tsx` only (the codebase already centralizes `HomeHero`/`HeroKpis` there; no new route or backend work is implied).\n- Anchor: `HeroKpis` (`index.tsx:322-414`), specifically the two-cell stat grid (`index.tsx:373-391`, `<HeroStatCell label=\"Healthy now\" .../>` and `<HeroStatCell label=\"Freshness\" .../>`). Reuse the existing `HeroStatCell` component (`index.tsx:436-493`) and `Sparkline` (`@/components/metagraphed/charts/sparkline`) \u2014 the same primitives already used for the Freshness cell \u2014 rather than inventing a new chart component.\n- Data source: call `chainActivityQuery(\"7d\")` (imported from `@/lib/metagraphed/queries`, same as `explorer.tsx:17`) inside `HeroKpis` via `useQuery` (matching the existing `coverageQuery`/`freshnessQuery`/`healthQuery` pattern at `index.tsx:323-325`, not `useSuspenseQuery`, so a slow/failed chain-activity fetch degrades gracefully instead of blocking the whole hero card). Read `activity.days` (`ChainActivityDay[]`, each with `block_count` / `extrinsic_count` / `event_count` / `successful_extrinsics` / `success_rate` / `unique_signers` \u2014 `apps/ui/src/lib/metagraphed/types.ts:1564-1579`), reverse it to chronological order (same `[...activity.days].reverse()` idiom as `explorer.tsx:236`), and feed one series (e.g. `extrinsic_count`, labeled to make clear it's chain-direct activity distinct from the registry \"Freshness\" cell) into a `Sparkline`.\n- What \"done\" looks like: the `HeroKpis` card gains a third stat cell (or extends the existing two-column grid to three) showing a current chain-activity value (e.g. latest day's extrinsic or block count) plus a small sparkline of the last N days, built the same honest-data way as the Freshness cell \u2014 no series renders when `chainActivityQuery` has no data yet (mirror the `hasSeries = !!series && series.length > 1` guard already in `HeroStatCell`, `index.tsx:454`), no fabricated fallback data.\n- Coordination note: this issue is one of 7 items under \"Charts & visualizations\" in the Wave 3 tracker (#2542); it is independent of its siblings (#3384-#3390) \u2014 no shared file or ordering dependency with those. It reuses the `Sparkline`/`HeroStatCell` primitives already present in `index.tsx`, so no coordination with `explorer.tsx` beyond copying its known-good `chainActivityQuery` usage pattern.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `apps/ui/src/routes/index.tsx` is the only source file changed (aside from an optional test file, if one is added)\n- [ ] `HeroKpis` calls `chainActivityQuery` (via `useQuery`, not `useSuspenseQuery`) and renders a new stat cell with a `Sparkline` driven by real `ChainActivityDay` data (e.g. `extrinsic_count` or `block_count`) \u2014 not by any hand-authored/mock array\n- [ ] The new cell hides its sparkline (renders no chart, or an appropriate empty/dash state) when the chain-activity query has no usable series, consistent with the \"no fabricated fallback\" pattern already used for the Freshness cell in the same component\n- [ ] No changes to `apps/ui/src/routes/explorer.tsx`, `queries.ts`, `types.ts`, or any backend/schema file \u2014 this PR is presentation-only, reusing existing query and chart primitives\n- [ ] `npm run build` / typecheck and lint pass with no new errors introduced in `apps/ui`\n- [ ] Before/after screenshots of the home page hero are included in the PR per the standing UI-change requirement (this touches visual output in `apps/ui/src/routes/index.tsx`)\n\n## Non-goals\n\n- Do not touch `apps/ui/src/routes/explorer.tsx` \u2014 its `MiniSeries`/chain-activity wiring is already correct and is not part of this change.\n- Do not add a new backend route or modify `chainActivityQuery`, `ChainActivity`, or any type in `queries.ts`/`types.ts` \u2014 the data layer is already wired and sufficient.\n- Do not build a full activity dashboard or multi-series chart on Home; this is a small hero-strip addition, not a port of the explorer page's \"Daily activity\" section.\n- Do not address any other \"Charts & visualizations\" sibling issue (#3384, #3385, #3386, #3388, #3389, #3390) in this PR \u2014 each is independently sized and scoped.\n\n## Size\n\nSize: S \u2014 keep this PR small (aim for \u226410 files / \u22641000 LOC).\n\nPart of #2542.",
